<title>UK: Social chapter would cost UK 500,000 jobs - Major.</title>
<headline>Social chapter would cost UK 500,000 jobs - Major.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Prime Minister John Major told parliament on Thursday that signing the European Union's social chapter would cost Britain half a million jobs.</p>
<p>&quot;We are not going to follow policies that would be damaging to British interests,&quot; he said at question time.  </p>
<p>Major said Britain intended to have its voice heard in Europe but would not slavishly follow policies, including social chapter legislation on workplace rules, that were against the national interest.</p>
<p>&quot;One signature on the Social Chapter will mean half a million signatures on the dole,&quot; Major said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44-171-542 7767</p>
